{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview","id":1097243,"title":"Shen Preview","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-26T13:02:51-07:00","id":1097243,"title":"Shen Preview","content":"Disclaimer: I will not and cannot represent the ideas and beliefs of the billions of people who are here now or have come before me in Chinese culture. I speak only for myself about the various elements of the preview that I find interesting or worth note. Hence, what I say is not ultimate truth, but merely an individual expression out of many.<br /> <br /> So the Shen Preview is certainly interesting, I want to see where it goes from here because there are some interesting gameplay elements that come about due to the shape of Chinese thought and understanding. Some things that I think work well are:<ul><li>Heaven as being part of the world, as realized in Chinese thought. Thank you for making that work.</li> <li>The idea that demons and titans can be made to harmonize with all things despite their disruptive tendencies. I realize that this is an adaption of Chinese thought to fit within the mechanics of the game. Some people will probably disagree about which entities are titans, primordials, gods, or just spirits. Chinese believers have similar arguments so to expect you to resolve that would be too much to ask.</li> <li>The Pantheon Path is interesting, but I would just like to note that despite appearances, we don't necessarily think of them as separate or opposite each other, which is why it is a single phrase whenever it is used in discourse. Ideally, I would prefer you to go through the entire process as you describe initially from the one to the ten thousand things, but considering how voluminous that is in Chinese culture, again too much to ask. Let's just hope people don't confuse yinyang for good and evil or right and wrong.</li> <li>Traditionalists and devoted followers will undoubtedly disagree about the divinity of great teachers such as Kong zi. But since you are attempting to add in all myths are true, this is perfectly acceptable to me, since it is the case that some believe them to have the spark of divinity. Again this is an argument of categorization which you won't be able to resolve.</li> <li>In general, the write ups for the gods are tasteful and respectful, while still retaining their identity which made them who they are. I have a few minor problems with certain gods and what they do in modern times. But I have a feeling that this might be the case with every Pantheon. How a god acts today is an interpretive endeavor, so I don't condemn this.</li> </ul>So here are my thoughts on this. I will say that this is much better than the Egyptian Preview which I felt was lacking in its own identity and borrowed too much from popular media interpretation or colonization.<br /> <br /> So what do you all think, either as a Chinese individual like myself, or as someone interested in mythology?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T14:01:07-07:00","id":1097284,"title":"","content":"Kong Zi being a god is a perfect example of how Scion is a setting based on mythology and not on religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T17:25:06-07:00","id":1097361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview#post1097243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]The Pantheon Path is interesting, but I would just like to note that despite appearances, we don't necessarily think of them as separate or opposite each other, which is why it is a single phrase whenever it is used in discourse. Ideally, I would prefer you to go through the entire process as you describe initially from the one to the ten thousand things, but considering how voluminous that is in Chinese culture, again too much to ask. Let's just hope people don't confuse yinyang for good and evil or right and wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>When we talk about Virtues, I went into some length about how they're not always diametrically opposed, but just often circling each other in conflict. The Norse with Fatalism and Audacity, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]Traditionalists and devoted followers will undoubtedly disagree about the divinity of great teachers such as Kong zi. But since you are attempting to add in all myths are true, this is perfectly acceptable to me, since it is the case that some believe them to have the spark of divinity. Again this is an argument of categorization which you won't be able to resolve. </div> </div> </div>Yeah. To be fair, nobody is angrier about him being a God than he himself. <br /> <br /> Thank you for your kind words!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T19:02:08-07:00","id":1097391,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know who the Palas are? They're mentioned as being a pantheon that shares Diyu with the Shen, Kami, and Deva.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T20:47:06-07:00","id":1097405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1097391#post1097391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know who the Palas are? They're mentioned as being a pantheon that shares Diyu with the Shen, Kami, and Deva.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well its Sanskrit, so I'd assume either a Vajrayana pantheon, or possible a Southeast Asian Pantheon assimilated into Buddhism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T21:41:13-07:00","id":1097414,"title":"","content":"The thing that's most clear to me, reading this preview? The guy who wrote it (If I'm reading the Kickstarter update right, it's a fellow named James Mendez Hodes) clearly loves his job, loved doing this, and had the BIGGEST grin when writing it up.<br /> <br /> As a guy who knew next to nothing about Chinese Myth outside of the main characters of Journey To The West, this was a fun read. With these Gods, I kind of want to make a Shen character now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T21:43:23-07:00","id":1097416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview#post1097243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what do you all think, either as a Chinese individual like myself, or as someone interested in mythology?</div> </div> </div> </div>Said it in another thread already, will say it again: I think it's the best Preview yet, in spite of some personal disagreements, and I'd be ecstatic if the whole book turned out like this. Every line of it shows enormous dedication.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T22:28:39-07:00","id":1097425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1097414#post1097414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that's most clear to me, reading this preview? The guy who wrote it (If I'm reading the Kickstarter update right, it's a fellow named James Mendez Hodes) clearly loves his job, loved doing this, and had the BIGGEST grin when writing it up.<br /> <br /> As a guy who knew next to nothing about Chinese Myth outside of the main characters of Journey To The West, this was a fun read. With these Gods, I kind of want to make a Shen character now.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might remember the author from the Exalted forum (&quot;what the Christ are you talking about?!&quot;), or from his comments here about scion in general and the Orisha (which I'm assuming he also wrote) in particular. It is the forum user Lula. I already knew a bit about Chinese mythology (hard not to stumble upon it when you study acupuncture) but it was a fun read to me as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","co