target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T01:03:21-07:00","id":1097452,"title":"","content":"'Air Traffic Control Constellation'<br /> <br /> This is the best thing ever and I want to shake your hand for writing it Lula.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T03:39:01-07:00","id":1097478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1097425#post1097425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might remember the author from the Exalted forum (&quot;what the Christ are you talking about?!&quot;), or from his comments here about scion in general and the Orisha (which I'm assuming he also wrote) in particular. It is the forum user Lula. I already knew a bit about Chinese mythology (hard not to stumble upon it when you study acupuncture) but it was a fun read to me as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Well, color me surprised.<br /> <br /> Lula! Awesome work!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T18:26:26-07:00","id":1097648,"title":"","content":"Well done, Lula. I loved the whole thing, and while the Air Traffic Contro Constellation got a solid chuckle I about died when I read the Wudang Clan section. Bravo, bravo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T19:49:49-07:00","id":1097670,"title":"","content":"I liked this preview a lot. The humor in it is great and the Shen are an interesting bunch.<br /> <br /> \u200bI love the idea that there's at least one Pantheon with genuinely different views about what to do about the Titans. (Yes, I noticed that the Orishas also differ from the norm as well.) I love the idea that the Shen consider 'reforming Titanspawn&quot; one of their big goals in the World.<br /> <br /> \u200bI like the &quot;Yin and Yang&quot; aspects of the Pantheon Paths. I've always been fascinated by the Yin/Yang duality, and this simple writeup put it in very easy-to-understand terms.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd what's this? A new All-Purpose Purview? I'm glad to see Beauty as a Purview unto itself, and I'm very curious to see how that shapes up.<br /> <br /> Good stuff all-around, here!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T21:47:54-07:00","id":1097687,"title":"","content":"I don't really like this one very much, to be honest.<br /> <br /> I'm not overly fond of the humor and how some of the deities wwere portrayed, but those are small problems that can be ignored. The big issues I have are that I feel like it's overly positive - like every other Pantheon, the Shen can be huge dickwads and I feel like, other than mentioning that they are often egotistical, this isn't really represented - and the presence of... how do I put it... I can't think of the right word, but the fact that there are sentences like &quot;...which Chang\u2019e herself attributes to the eyes of sexism on a woman who knows what she wants...&quot; or &quot;...he\u2019s realized how much toxic masculinity colors his actions and feelings.&quot; displease me.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's just because I lean further towards cynical side of the spectrum in regards to how the gods behave than most people on this forum seem to, but this one didn't sit right with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T21:50:58-07:00","id":1097688,"title":"","content":"I think I'm gonna cut the toxic masculinity line. I actually forget why I put it in. I think it was supposed to be the intro to a paragraph that I ran out of space for, and now it seems kinda random.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T01:00:39-07:00","id":1097710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1097687#post1097687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really like this one very much, to be honest.<br /> <br /> I'm not overly fond of the humor and how some of the deities wwere portrayed, but those are small problems that can be ignored. The big issues I have are that I feel like it's overly positive - like every other Pantheon, the Shen can be huge dickwads and I feel like, other than mentioning that they are often egotistical, this isn't really represented - and the presence of... how do I put it... I can't think of the right word, but the fact that there are sentences like &quot;...which Chang\u2019e herself attributes to the eyes of sexism on a woman who knows what she wants...&quot; or &quot;...he\u2019s realized how much toxic masculinity colors his actions and feelings.&quot; displease me.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's just because I lean further towards cynical side of the spectrum in regards to how the gods behave than most people on this forum seem to, but this one didn't sit right with me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I readily admit that it seems very light and romantic, but this is something that Chinese authors do as well. The past and myths are told in mostly positive lights in favor of the good deities over the disreputable ones, until they get better and then they are seen positively as well. Some contemporaries argue that harmony is just a nice way of explaining things we don't understand. Or that such order is actually deceptive of what is really a chaotic existence. <br /> <br /> But I don't mind the levity, even if it is deceptive, simply because it matches the human ability to do the same. And a pleasant face can be much more sinister when it hides an ugly heart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T04:22:13-07:00","id":1097741,"title":"","content":"This preview once again Highlights the improvements I love about 2nd ed Scion! YanluoWang/Yama existing in multiple pantheons, which I used in the previous Scion Edition, rather then had him be multiple gods.<br /> <br /> Though I am confused, so since Plains enter into Tian, and see pagodas that means the World does know about magic and the Gods? I thought it was a half secret?<br /> <br /> I am really digging the Pai Mei as a Titan, this is the stuff I encourage, making famous villains reflective in the gameline's personal mythology.<br /> <br /> So Beauty is available to all Pantheons right? Like they added it later into the gameline when tweaking things right? Or is it the Pantheon Power of the Shen?<br /> <br /> So the 8 Immortals, and Qin Shi Huangdi are likely gods now I take it. Other potential gods I'm thinking of is Li Bai the famous Poet and Academician. Zhang Fei and Liu Bei, who I'm thinking at the very least were made Demigod level as brothers of Guan Yu. Lu Bu, cause come on you know everyone has fun with the very idea of that guy, for the same reason we like Pai Mei.<br /> <br /> And Guanyin, so it seems ambiguous and referred to mostly as they, and once as her in the preview. So will they be either sex among the Shen or female among the Shen and male among the older buddhists of the Devas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T04:28:54-07:00","id":1097747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1097741#post1097741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Beauty is available to all Pantheons right? Like they added it later into the gameline when tweaking things right? Or is it the Pantheon Power of the Shen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tianmeng is the Shen's Pantheon Purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T06:23:37-07:00","id":1097760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1097741#post1097741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This preview once again Highlights the improvements I love about 2nd ed Scion! YanluoWang/Yama existing in multiple pantheons, which I used in the previous Scion Edition, rather then had him be multiple gods.<br /> <br /> Though I am confused, so since Plains enter into Tian, and see pagodas that means the World does know about magic and the Gods? I thought it was a half secret?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that it is supposed to be a secret. I think it makes sense for certain belief systems to make things much more of an open secret. It really depends on how many adherents they actually have and what they might believe in. Worship doesn't give more power to gods, but it certainly gives them breathing room since they don't have to keep as many secrets.<br /> <br /> Like most people in my region of the world, I personally believe in a large number of various teachings from multiple schools of thought, but I don't display this as a matter of faith, merely an acceptance of existence. I ring the fortune bells, and purchase the dao prayer strips. I pray and acknowledge various deities according to custom. Chinese New Year is important so I have to avoid cleaning the house for that period. I grew up in a house with a shrine in one corner, so I have one in my house as well. <br /> <br /> So am I superstitious to believe in such silly notions and rituals when I should focus on the facts and logic of our world? Or perhaps I find nothing wrong about accepting them both at the same time.<br /> <br /> Never underestimate the human ability to cope with paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T10:35:45-07:00","id":1097820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1097760#post1097760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never underestimate the human ability to cope with paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember someone saying that they couldn't understand how supernatural stuff could stay hidden and people could stay oblivious in urban fantasy stuff.<br /> <br /> My immediate snapback to that was &quot;So how many people are adamant that Pluto's still a planet, or that dinosaurs didn't have feathers?&quot;<br /> <br /> You don't even need to get into religious belief to find people who respond to facts that contradict their worldview by covering their ears and yelling &quot;LALALALALA&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T16:21:07-07:00","id":1097898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1097820#post1097820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember someone saying that they couldn't understand how supernatural stuff could stay hidden and people could stay oblivious in urban fantasy stuff.<br /> <br /> My immediate snapback to that was &amp;quot;So how many people are adamant that Pluto's still a planet, or that dinosaurs didn't have feathers?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> You don't even need to get into religious belief to find people who respond to facts that contradict their worldview by covering their ears and yelling &amp;quot;LALALALALA&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between &quot;scientists say x about a thing the public cannot actually see&quot; and &quot;demigod picks up a truck and throws it at the flaming T-Rex while being filmed by thirty phones&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T16:59:44-07:00","id":1097903,"title":"","content":"They've stated a couple of times that in the default 2e setting magic and such isn't really secret at all. There's no veil or myst, or anything like that. Gods and scions are a known factor.<br /> <br /> Neall talked about it a bit, much better than I just did: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1038761-how-much-do-people-actually-know-of-mythic-reality?p=1038820#post1038820\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...20#post1038820</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T17:03:33-07:00","id":1097904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1097898#post1097898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a difference between &quot;scientists say x about a thing the public cannot actually see&quot; and &quot;demigod picks up a truck and throws it at the flaming T-Rex while being filmed by thirty phones&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There are people who insist that the Earth is flat.<br /> <br /> <i>I have learned there is no bottom of the barrel for human ignorance</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T17:37:25-07:00","id":1097915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1097904#post1097904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are people who insist that the Earth is flat.<br /> <br /> <i>I have learned there is no bottom of the barrel for human ignorance</i></div> </div> </div> </div>1) extreme minority<br /> <br /> 2) not denying what is nakedly in front of them; from casual human perception the world does seem to a plane around them, so not comparable to people witnessing the supernatural and living in denial","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-28-2017, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T20:04:43-07:00","id":1097946,"title":"","content":"Eh, nevermind. Continue!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T03:03:31-07:00","id":1100057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalicWanderer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1097903#post1097903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've stated a couple of times that in the default 2e setting magic and such isn't really secret at all. There's no veil or myst, or anything like that. Gods and scions are a known factor.<br /> <br /> Neall talked about it a bit, much better than I just did: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1038761-how-much-do-people-actually-know-of-mythic-reality?p=1038820#post1038820\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...20#post1038820</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The feeling I got was sort of a , &quot;They are known if you know where to look, but most people don't know where to look&quot;. I mean you might accept that, yes that thing does look like a hydra, that's probably where the Greeks got the idea from. That's a far cry from &quot;Zeus is real and wants to bang my wife&quot;. The gods and supernaturals don't hide, but fatebinding is a thing so they don't really go out of their way to flaunt their power to non-believers if there's not a reason to. A dreamcatcher might be stopping evil spirits but the user assumes it's a placebo effect. People disappear on the hill with the old mansion where all those murders happened thirty yers ago, no I don't know why just stay away.<br /> <br /> Much like real life where people don't always question why something works even if they know for a fact it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T13:36:45-07:00","id":1100201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1100057#post1100057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The feeling I got was sort of a , &quot;They are known if you know where to look, but most people don't know where to look&quot;. I mean you might accept that, yes that thing does look like a hydra, that's probably where the Greeks got the idea from. That's a far cry from &quot;Zeus is real and wants to bang my wife&quot;. The gods and supernaturals don't hide, but fatebinding is a thing so they don't really go out of their way to flaunt their power to non-believers if there's not a reason to. A dreamcatcher might be stopping evil spirits but the user assumes it's a placebo effect. People disappear on the hill with the old mansion where all those murders happened thirty yers ago, no I don't know why just stay away.<br /> <br /> Much like real life where people don't always question why something works even if they know for a fact it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, it's a bit like that, but the person probably wouldn't assume it's a placebo. To wit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1025236#post1025236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>\u201cOnce upon a time,\u201d says the storyteller. People in our world hear the phrase and know it means \u201ca long time ago,\u201d or \u201cbefore things were the way they are today,\u201d or \u201cin the beginning.\u201d<br /> In the World, \u201conce upon a time\u201d was last week, and everyone's still watching the story unfold on the evening news. In the World, legends weren't just made back in the day before video cameras and the internet. They're striding down the streets downtown right now, and #TeamTezcatlipoca is trending on Twitter. In the World, nobody disputes the wisdom of knocking on wood to ward off malignant spirits, because malignant spirits spew out of the Axis Mundi next door all the time. Inhabitants of the World wake up to just a little more wonder and a few more omens every morning.<br /> <br /> That's not to say the curtain between the mundane and the divine is shredded daily, or even often. Most people never see a God in the flesh. They work, party, study, travel, and make love without any overt interference from mystical forces nine times out of ten. But mystical forces live in their neighborhoods, and that tenth time could be the one to tangle a person's Fate up in something much bigger than herself.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Whether it's knocking on wood, having a dreamcatcher or tossing a pinch of salt over your shoulder, people generally understand that this isn't superstition, it's caution. Sure, you could do without the dreamcatcher and most nights you'll be fine, just like you could ride a bike without a helmet. But everyone knows it could end badly, and the one time it does...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T16:50:15-07:00","id":1100259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1100201#post1100201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWell, it's a bit like that, but the person probably wouldn't assume it's a placebo. To wit:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Whether it's knocking on wood, having a dreamcatcher or tossing a pinch of salt over your shoulder, people generally understand that this isn't superstition, it's caution. Sure, you could do without the dreamcatcher and most nights you'll be fine, just like you could ride a bike without a helmet. But everyone knows it could end badly, and the one time it does...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah fair enough, I forgot that particular quote. So I suppose it would lay more along the lines of taking measures against a bear attack, no it's probably never going to happen to you or anyone you know. but it's not unthinkable and you'd be rather put out if it did.<br /> <br /> Though I imagine it would probably straddle a weird line between people that are all about the folklore elements and the people that do dismiss it as superstition, not because it doesn't work but because there &quot;must&quot; be a scientific reason evil spirits don't like salt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","user":"vonpenguin","date":". 06-04-2017, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T12:29:29-07:00","id":1100528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1100259#post1100259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah fair enough, I forgot that particular quote. So I suppose it would lay more along the lines of taking measures against a bear attack, no it's probably never going to happen to you or anyone you know. but it's not unthinkable and you'd be rather put out if it did.<br /> <br /> Though I imagine it would probably straddle a weird line between people that are all about the folklore elements and the people that do dismiss it as superstition, not because it doesn't work but because there &quot;must&quot; be a scientific reason evil spirits don't like salt.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAs has been noted quite often, there are real people who think the Earth is flat. There will always be those who insist one thing or another regardless of sense, reason or evidence. Ignoring the outliers, though, I figure most people do what makes sense to them, just as they do in our world. Only difference is that things we might consider to be simple superstition makes a lot of sense. Again, nine out of ten people will never witness any big, mythic stuff outside of the news, but your neighborhood probably has a satyr living in a small apartment, constantly being told off for his loud music and bringing something new to every Saturday night poetry jam. <br /> <br /> \u200bWhat I'm not entirely clear on is whether people know he's a satyr, since apparently they can look quite human. Does he just not have hooves or horns? I'm still figuring that part out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T13:26:45-07:00","id":1100551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1100528#post1100528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bAs has been noted quite often, there are real people who think the Earth is flat. There will always be those who insist one thing or another regardless of sense, reason or evidence. Ignoring the outliers, though, I figure most people do what makes sense to them, just as they do in our world. Only difference is that things we might consider to be simple superstition makes a lot of sense. Again, nine out of ten people will never witness any big, mythic stuff outside of the news, but your neighborhood probably has a satyr living in a small apartment, constantly being told off for his loud music and bringing something new to every Saturday night poetry jam.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat I'm not entirely clear on is whether people know he's a satyr, since apparently they can look quite human. Does he just not have hooves or horns? I'm still figuring that part out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah wasn't arguing that point, just noting there would probably be a divide on people that think mystical is &quot;science we don't understand yet&quot; and just take it in stride.<br /> <br /> And the ones that think the gods are alien lizard men secretly controlling the illumanati through flu shots.<br /> <br /> Maybe depends on the variety of Satyr, since they can presumably interbreed with humans how strong the blood is might come into play? He might just be fond of jaunty hats and baggy pants so you can't quite tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T08:45:48-07:00","id":1100858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1100551#post1100551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the ones that think the gods are alien lizard men secretly controlling the illumanati through flu shots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure as to details yet but I am stealing this for an adventure hook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T06:04:37-07:00","id":1129198,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry because this is very late, but ... has anybody noticed that the Jade Emperor doesn't have his own write-up in the Shen Preview? This is very confusing to me, since he's mentioned as Erlang's uncle, Nuwa's father and the head of the celestial bureaucracy, but his Callings and Purviews are never mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12342-dr-quantum","name":"Dr. Quantum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T01:16:39-07:00","id":1129713,"title":"","content":"Maybe he's a distant father, or not too interested in having progeny these days?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:35:45-07:00","id":1132059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr. Quantum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097243-shen-preview?p=1129198#post1129198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry because this is very late, but ... has anybody noticed that the Jade Emperor doesn't have his own write-up in the Shen Preview? This is very confusing to me, since he's mentioned as Erlang's uncle, Nuwa's father and the head of the celestial bureaucracy, but his Callings and Purviews are never mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the Jade Emperor, like the other two Pure Ones, is a Primordial. I did kind of like the First Edition notion that it's a position rather than an individual, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}